  "body": "Tool library import can't update or replace tools; it only adds or renames them.\n\n**Where:** `ImportTools` (`crates/app/src/commands/tool_import.rs:81-86`) skips an identical tool and RENAMES a same-named different one (`A (2)`). There's no replace or update mode, and no key but the name.\n\n**Effect:** re-importing an updated library (e.g. after a feeds-and-speeds revision) adds a renamed duplicate of every changed tool, instead of updating them. *Guess:* that's every tool in a library-wide feeds change.\n\n**Fix sketch:** an import mode with three options: add (today's behaviour), update matching tools, or replace. Matching is by name, or by part number once tools carry one (see the tool-metadata issue filed alongside this). It's one undoable command, with a preview of what changes. Add it to MCP too.\n\nEffort: medium.\n\n**Done means:** re-importing a revised library updates matching tools in place, with one undo; pinned.\n",
